<article class="env-example" id="06BN">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06BN">Example <span data-tag="06BN">7.6.6.34</span>.</a> Let $\mathbb {K}$ be a collection of simplicial sets and let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an inner fibration of $\infty $-categories. Then $U$ is $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete if and only if satisfies the following condition: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
For each $K \in \mathbb {K}$ and each object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, every diagram $f: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C}$ can be extended to a colimit diagram $\overline{f}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C}$, which is also a $U$-colimit diagram in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> See Proposition <a data-tag="05J6" href="/tag/05J6">7.1.7.14</a>. </p>
</article>
